From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView: Apply farbling seeds before renderer-initiated
 navigations

Page::set_farbling_seed only stores the seed for documents created after
it arrives. Copying onto live documents rewrote the outgoing page during
cross-site navigation. Top-level navigations, including location.href,
link clicks, and history traversal, now send the destination site's seed
before the new document is created. A self-navigating iframe keeps the
top site's seed.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/Page/Page.cpp                |  4 ----
 Libraries/LibWebView/CanonicalNavigable.cpp   |  2 ++
 Libraries/LibWebView/CanonicalTraversable.cpp |  4 ++++
 Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.cpp       | 13 +++++++++++++
 Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.h         |  1 +
 5 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/Page/Page.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/Page/Page.cpp
index 2e6ce1e0b252e6c203d845872e0e2274f8042719..87623eee472823158b0944681a6ac608c4ce9d90 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/Page/Page.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/Page/Page.cpp
@@ -136,10 +136,6 @@ Compositor::CompositorHost const& Page::compositor_host() const
 void Page::set_farbling_seed(Farbling::Seed seed)
 {
     m_farbling_seed = seed;
-    for (auto navigable : hosted_navigables()) {
-        if (auto document = navigable->active_document())
-            document->relevant_settings_object().set_farbling_seed(seed);
-    }
 }
 
 void Page::visit_edges(JS::Cell::Visitor& visitor)
diff --git a/Libraries/LibWebView/CanonicalNavigable.cpp b/Libraries/LibWebView/CanonicalNavigable.cpp
index be722edd5aee951f63aaaacca960fd1f2acb69a1..575fec085e22f5d334718a7a3209876bf0e2d2fc 100644
